t helps downstream. I'll add attribute \"bore_type\" values string full/reduced. 32 entries again... That's a 7th attribute. Length grows. Alternatively rely on matrix rows with bore_type column. I'll include bore_type in matrix rows only, skip as model_level. Hmm — consistency: model_level should let you query per model. I'll include it; strings short.\n\nActually, to control output size, maybe I skip diameter in model_level (it's in matrix tables and derivable from DN label). But rules emphasize model_level population... I'll include everything; better complete. The JSON will be long but fine.\n\nmatrix_tables: two entries as planned, with columns and column_units.\n\nFootnote: marker \"*\", text as extracted. Also attach footnote_markers to RB rows? Footnote markers per row — rows are objects; I can add \"footnote_markers\": [\"*\"] to RB rows. I'll add to the four RB rows in table 3.\n\nThe notes after tables (\"Please note that the flow rates...\") — conditions. Could go into matrix_tables description or footnotes. I'll include a condensed version in each matrix table's \"description\". Description for table 2: \"Flow rates Q1, Q2, Q3, Q4 can be freely chosen: Q3 and ratio Q3/Q1 selected per OIML R49-1:2013(E); Q1, Q2 are minimum values with Q2/Q1 = 1.6; Q3, Q4 are maximum values with Q4/Q3 = 1.25; Q3/Q1 at least 40.\" Something like that. Also for table 3 same.\n\nTest reports: five entries, role \"type_evaluation_report\"? Let me choose \"test_report\". Hmm. The certificate page 2: \"The conformity was established by the results of tests and examinations provided in the associated reports\". Under scheme A, NMi is both issuer and evaluator; these reports are the Type Evaluation Report(s). Page 1 mentions \"the OIML Type Evaluation Report\". Given five reports listed, they collectively form the evaluation. I'll assign role \"type_evaluation_report\" to all five. Also documentation file T10554-5 with role \"documentation_file\", id \"T10554-5\". The text: \"The