"T10554-5\", \"role\": \"documentation_file\"} — no date/pages. Schema allows omitting absent fields (rule 8).\n\nNow writing values precisely with decimal points.\n\nAlso note: class 1 DN600 Q1 \"50,400\" → 50.4; Q2 \"80,640\" → 80.64. Class 2 DN100 RB Q2 \"1,00\" → 1.\n\nLet me carefully produce the models list (32):\n\nclass1: DN50-class1, DN65-class1, DN80-class1, DN100-class1, DN125-class1, DN150-class1, DN200-class1, DN250-class1, DN300-class1, DN350-class1, DN400-class1, DN450-class1, DN500-class1, DN600-class1 (14)\n\nclass2: DN50-class2, DN50-RB-class2, DN65-class2, DN65-RB-class2, DN80-class2, DN80-RB-class2, DN100-class2, DN100-RB-class2, DN125-class2, DN150-class2, DN200-class2, DN250-class2, DN300-class2, DN350-class2, DN400-class2, DN450-class2, DN500-class2, DN600-class2 (18)\n\nTotal 32. \n\nmodels[] with attributes:\n{\"model_id\": \"DN50-class1\", \"attributes\": {\"meter_size\": \"DN50\", \"accuracy_class\": 1, \"bore_type\": \"full\"}}\n... etc.\nRB ones: bore_type \"reduced\", meter_size \"DN50 RB\"? or \"DN50\"? The inscription identity is \"DNxxx RB\". I'll set meter_size \"DN50 RB\". Hmm, model label \"DN50-RB-class2\". attributes meter_size: \"DN50 RB\". Fine.\n\nNow write model_level arrays. Let me tabulate all again for accuracy (class, size, dia, q1, q2, q3, q4, ratio):\n\n1: DN50-class1: 50, 0.315, 0.504, 63, 78.75, 200\n2: DN65-class1: 65, 0.5, 0.8, 100, 125, 200\n3: DN80-class1: 80, 0.8, 1.28, 160, 200, 200\n4: DN100-class1: 100, 1, 1.6, 250, 312.5, 250\n5: DN125-class1: 125, 1.6, 2.56, 400, 500, 250\n6: DN150-class1: 150, 3.9375, 6.3, 630, 787.5, 160\n7: DN200-class1: 200, 6.25, 10, 1000, 1250, 160\n8: DN250-class1: 250, 10, 16, 1600, 2000, 160\n9: DN300-class1: 300, 15.625, 25, 2500, 3125, 160\n10: DN350-class1: 350, 15.625, 25, 2500, 3125, 160\n11: DN400-class1: 400, 25, 40, 4000, 5000, 160\n12: DN450-class1: 450, 39.375, 63, 6300, 7875, 160\n13: DN500-class1: 500, 39.375, 63, 6300, 7875, 160\n14: DN600-class1: 600, 50.4, 80.64, 630